---
/**
 * A text block's content with NO element around it — used by Quotation.astro for the
 * attribution, whose element is the `<figcaption>` it is rendered into.
 *
 * ── WHY NOT LET IT BE A <p> ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * `<p>` inside `<figcaption>` is valid HTML, and it is what the attribution would be if
 * it were simply restyled `normal`. It breaks two things:
 *
 *   - The en dash. Quotation writes it before the block, so a `<p>` would put the dash
 *     on a line of its own, above the name.
 *   - The right edge. base.css caps every `.detail p` at 66ch, and `ch` resolves
 *     against the element's own font — the caption's 16px, not the body's 20. So the
 *     `<p>` would be narrower than the figure it sits in, and an end-aligned line would
 *     end short of the quote's edge. DESIGN.md excludes `figcaption` from the cap for
 *     exactly this reason; a `<p>` inside one would bring it back.
 *
 * `index` and `isInline` arrive in props and are not destructured — nothing reads them,
 * and neither does `node`. The library has already built the marks tree into the slot.
 */
---

<slot />
